## Tier Limit Enforcement

Every API route and Server Action that processes a query MUST check tier limits first.

```typescript
import { enforceTierLimit } from '@/lib/tier-enforcement'

// In route handler or server action:
const { allowed, used, limit } = await enforceTierLimit(tenantId)

if (!allowed) {
  return {
    status:  'error',
    code:    'TIER_LIMIT_EXCEEDED',
    message: `Monthly limit of ${limit} queries reached. Upgrade to continue.`,
  }
}
```

### Tier limits reference
```
free:       500  queries/month  — $0
starter:    10_000             — $149
growth:     50_000             — $499
enterprise: unlimited          — custom
```

